				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/bafkreieroaneiobsowwop7dvxchj6kofurkgo5mupns5yuagvrjg7y2jsy"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-17T16:33:44.414Z",
			"content": "<p>I found original favicon. It was lost on September 4th!<br>\n<a href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20250903201138/https://www.microsoft.com/favicon.ico\">web.archive.org/web/20250903...</a></p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2biavsmk2n",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2azm6wqs23",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com/post/3lz2biavsmk2n",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/zachleat.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/bafkreie4yypxcxrte6shppdo6glzt7gtmueprazp3xndeksuw2uid2ecfm"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-17T16:38:05.971Z",
			"content": "<p>fwiw I tested in plenty of hardware/software/VPN combinations</p>\n<p>the problem is that <a href=\"https://microsoft.com\">microsoft.com</a> points to <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/favicon.ico?v2\">www.microsoft.com/favicon.ico?v2</a> in markup (which is a corrupted icon per multiple image editing tools I tested)</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:pkzt5mk76dc3fnd7w7l7veyr/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2bnww4kc2w",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:nejscld5zlavytijxz27qhvj/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2axj4sxs2i",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/rreverser.com/post/3lz2bnww4kc2w",
			"author": {
				"name": "Ingvar Stepanyan",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/rreverser.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:pkzt5mk76dc3fnd7w7l7veyr/bafkreiav6mrc4pmvkth5jvs6kayu6omnpdvpnvgvi2aywcgmykyo6wirby"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-17T16:41:16.822Z",
			"content": "<p>Doesn't work for me either, <a href=\"https://www.microsoft.com/favicon.ico\">www.microsoft.com/favicon.ico</a> returns a clearly broken image file.</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2br6xwb22z",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2bahhqtk23",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/alexdln.com/post/3lz2br6xwb22z",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/alexdln.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/bafkreieroaneiobsowwop7dvxchj6kofurkgo5mupns5yuagvrjg7y2jsy"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-17T16:43:05.933Z",
			"content": "<p>What's more, the problem isn't related to the tests (at least not the actual testing) or query parameters. On September 3rd, the file with ?v2 was still working. Then either they updated the response of this file, or they simply lost the files.</p>\n<p>I don't know why I checked this 😅</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
		{
			"id": "at://did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2buugioc2i",
			"parentId": "at://did:plc:xpchjovbk6sxl3bv74z7cs54/app.bsky.feed.post/3lz2biavsmk2n",
			"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/alexdln.com/post/3lz2buugioc2i",
			"author": {
				"name": "Alex",
				"url": "https://bsky.app/profile/alexdln.com",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/avatar/plain/did:plc:er6erflnnxcozlbqmrpflt6h/bafkreieroaneiobsowwop7dvxchj6kofurkgo5mupns5yuagvrjg7y2jsy"
			},
			"date": "2025-09-17T16:45:09.094Z",
			"content": "<p>This is more a question for those who have it working.</p>\n<p>The favicon is usually cached for a year, so it's displayed for many. Although, it's possible in some countries it's cached at the CDN level and is still being served...</p>",
			"via": "bluesky"
		},
